## 1. Baseline Pipeline — What the Human Built

This section documents the existing, human-authored pipeline extracted directly from the codebase.

### 1.1 Data Loading & Cleaning ([shared/dataset_loader.py](file:///d:/2025/AgentDS/AgentDSSimulators/agentds-platform/backend/healthcare/shared/dataset_loader.py), [shared/preprocessing.py](file:///d:/2025/AgentDS/AgentDSSimulators/agentds-platform/backend/healthcare/shared/preprocessing.py))

| Step | Implementation |
|------|----------------|
| **Data source** | Local CSV → HuggingFace fallback (`lainmn/AgentDS-Healthcare`) |
| **Deduplication** | `df.drop_duplicates()` |
| **ID column removal** | Heuristic: drop columns where `nunique == len(df)` |
| **Patient join** | Optional left-merge with `patients.csv` on `subject_id` (readmission only) |

### 1.2 Feature Engineering

> [!WARNING]
> [features.py](file:///d:/2025/AgentDS/AgentDSSimulators/agentds-platform/backend/healthcare/discharge_readiness/model/features.py) in all three problem statements contains **empty lists** (`NUMERIC_FEATURES = []`, `CATEGORICAL_FEATURES = []`). Feature groups are **not explicitly defined** — all features are auto-inferred from dtype.

- **Numeric features**: Auto-detected via `df.select_dtypes(include=['int64','float64'])`
- **Categorical features**: Auto-detected via `df.select_dtypes(include=['object','category','bool'])`
- **No domain-specific engineering**: No derived features (e.g., length of stay, age bins, comorbidity scores, prior visit counts)

### 1.3 Preprocessing Pipeline ([shared/preprocessing.py](file:///d:/2025/AgentDS/AgentDSSimulators/agentds-platform/backend/healthcare/shared/preprocessing.py))

```python
# Numeric
SimpleImputer(strategy='median') → StandardScaler()

# Categorical
SimpleImputer(strategy='constant', fill_value='missing') → OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore')

# Combined via ColumnTransformer (remainder='drop')
```

### 1.4 Model Architecture

| Task | Model | Parameters |
|------|-------|------------|
| Readmission Prediction | `RandomForestClassifier` | `n_estimators=100, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1` |
| ED Cost Forecasting | `RandomForestRegressor` | `n_estimators=100, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1` |
| Discharge Readiness | `RandomForestClassifier` | `n_estimators=100, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1` |

> [!NOTE]
> All three tasks share **identical default hyperparameters**. No tuning is performed.

### 1.5 Training Pipeline

```
Load Data → clean_data() → train_test_split(test_size=0.2, random_state=42)
         → ColumnTransformer → RandomForest → fit() → predict()
```

- **No cross-validation**: Single 80/20 holdout split
- **No stratified split**: `stratify=None` in `train_test_split`
- **No imbalance handling**: No SMOTE, no class weights, no threshold tuning

### 1.6 Evaluation Metrics

| Task Type | Metrics Tracked |
|-----------|----------------|
| Classification (Readmission, Discharge) | `macro_f1`, `weighted_f1` |
| Regression (ED Cost) | `MAE`, `RMSE`, `R²` |

> [!WARNING]
> **Missing critical metrics**:
> - Classification: No `AUC-ROC`, no `precision`, no `recall`, no `AUPRC` (important for imbalanced data)
> - Regression: No `MAPE`, no `median AE`, no prediction interval calibration

