## 6. Risks & Limitations

| Risk | Description | Mitigation |
|------|-------------|------------|
| **Data leakage** | Derived features (e.g., prior visit count) may encode future info if not computed on training partition only | Compute aggregations using only pre-admission data; apply feature engineering inside CV folds |
| **SMOTE with categorical** | Standard SMOTE doesn't handle mixed data | Use `SMOTENC` specifying which columns are categorical |
| **Log transform bias** | `log1p` back-transform introduces bias in expected value | Report both log-scale and original-scale metrics; consider bias correction |
| **Calibration validity** | Isotonic calibration requires enough minority class samples | Use only if minority class > ~200 samples |
| **Overfitting (XGBoost/LGBM)** | Boosting can overfit on small datasets | Use early stopping + CV; monitor train vs. val loss gap |
| **Distributional shift** | Model trained on one hospital may generalize poorly | Report results per demographic subgroup; use cross-site validation if available |
| **No clinical validation** | ML metrics (AUC) don't guarantee clinical utility | Add decision curve analysis (DCA) and net benefit curve |
| **Missing features.py** | All [features.py](file:///d:/2025/AgentDS/AgentDSSimulators/agentds-platform/backend/healthcare/discharge_readiness/model/features.py) files are empty — no schema documentation | Populate with actual column names post EDA for validation and reproducibility |

